# TidyMac Windows — Agent Workflow Guide

You are working on **TidyMac Windows** — a native Windows PC cleaner (Tauri + Rust core + Vue 3 + Bun).

## Mandatory reading
Always read `AGENTS.md` before making any change. It defines safety boundaries, architecture rules, and engineering method.

## Commands (type these to trigger the workflow)

| Trigger | What happens |
|---------|-------------|
| `@next` or "what's next" | Read `docs/windows/NEXT-STEPS.md`, find top Phase 7 TODO, output action plan |
| `@discover` or "find features" | Scan parity gaps, unregistered specs, Windows-specific ideas, UX backlog, & competitor patterns → discovery report |
| `@spec <TM-WIN-ID>` | Research spec, find similar existing tool, produce plan — no code yet |
| `@implement <feature>` | Full TDD workflow: register → failing test → implement → wire → validate → update docs |
| `@validate` | Run `cargo test --workspace && bun run test`, report results |
| `@safety-check` | Audit open files/diff for Windows safety invariants |
| `@review` | Structured review: blocking safety, spec compliance, test coverage, code quality |

## Quick facts
- **Toolchain:** `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` (MinGW at `F:\Project\Programs\msys64\`)
- **All 6 phases complete** — next work is Phase 7 (`docs/windows/NEXT-STEPS.md`)
- **Priority 1:** AI Clutter scanner (TM-WIN-AICLUTTER-01)
- **Priority 2:** Cloud Cleanup / OneDrive (TM-WIN-CLOUD-01)
- **Validation:** `.\scripts\validate-windows.ps1` or `cargo test --workspace`

## Hard rules (never violate)
- No `fs::remove_file` / `DeleteFileW` directly — always use `mover_windows.rs`
- No hardcoded localized folder names — always `SHGetKnownFolderPath(FOLDERID_*)`
- No telemetry, background processes, or network calls
- Nothing pre-ticked in scan result UI
- Platform gates: `#[cfg(target_os = "windows")]` / `#[cfg(target_os = "macos")]`
- Unavailable features → explicit `ComingSoon` or error — never silent no-op

